title: Guard the smoke fork probe's PAR_TEMP prefix check against an unset PAR_TEMP
updated: 2026-11-07T04:07:02Z
---

Found by mcp-hub-binary-worker during k162. scripts/smoke-binary.sh:357, the fork probe, checks index($r->{from} // "", "$ENV{PAR_TEMP}/") == 0. If PAR_TEMP were unset, the prefix becomes "/" and the check passes for any absolute path, so a module loaded from a host perl would count as "from the archive". Inside the binary PAR_TEMP is always set, so this does not misfire today. The new JSON check from k162 already guards it with length($par). Done when the fork probe has the same guard (an unset or empty PAR_TEMP fails the check) and smoke-binary.sh still passes on a real build. Lane: mcp-hub-binary-worker.
